WEBVTT

00:06.440 --> 00:09.480
Thank you for coming, Subaru-kun.

00:09.480 --> 00:13.990
Nice to meet you.
I'm Maho-Maho's father, Misawa Fuuga.

00:14.990 --> 00:16.410
Right...

00:23.080 --> 00:26.080
Um, what is going on here?

00:26.080 --> 00:29.290
I need to thank you for all the care you've given Maho-Maho,

00:29.630 --> 00:31.880
but today's a special day!

00:35.970 --> 00:40.350
Congratulations! Misawa Maho and Hasegawa Subaru's Marriage Reception!

00:36.300 --> 00:38.220
Wh-What?!

00:38.220 --> 00:40.350
Congratulations, Maho-Maho, Subaru-kun.

00:41.100 --> 00:42.470
M-Marriage?

00:42.470 --> 00:44.730
Maho! What exactly is going on here?

00:44.730 --> 00:48.770
I-I'm marrying Subaru-kun? I had no idea!

00:49.980 --> 00:54.190
"Konnyaku?" You mean like that delicious oden with miso on top?

00:54.190 --> 00:55.320
That "Konnyaku?"

00:55.320 --> 00:56.570
Oh!

00:56.570 --> 00:58.740
That's "Konjac!"

00:58.740 --> 00:59.910
Oh?

00:59.910 --> 01:02.450
Was I wrong, Maho-Maho?

01:02.450 --> 01:06.000
Father! There's so many things wrong here!

01:06.000 --> 01:08.330
Subarun belongs to everyone!

01:08.330 --> 01:11.170
He'll marry everyone, if that's the case!

01:11.790 --> 01:14.550
That's wrong, too!

01:16.210 --> 01:17.800
I see.

01:17.800 --> 01:21.720
Maho-Maho is always so happy when she's talking about you.

01:21.720 --> 01:25.100
I thought you two were very close already.

01:26.140 --> 01:27.810
C-Close?

01:28.140 --> 01:30.150
Sorry, Subaru-kun.

01:30.150 --> 01:35.440
Putting marriage aside, I've
always wanted to meet you.

01:47.450 --> 01:49.960
Wh-What is it?

01:50.370 --> 01:54.960
Yeah, Maho-Maho is right.
You're a fabulous young man.

01:55.340 --> 01:58.630
I can leave Maho-Maho to you with no worries.

01:58.630 --> 02:00.760
Thank you very much.

02:00.760 --> 02:04.600
I told you! Subarun's the best coach!

02:04.600 --> 02:05.680
Right, everyone?

02:05.680 --> 02:06.220
Yeah!

02:06.220 --> 02:07.640
Yes, of course!

02:07.640 --> 02:08.520
Oh!

02:08.520 --> 02:09.980
Onii-chan's the best!

02:09.980 --> 02:11.560
Yeah, the best!

02:13.020 --> 02:14.730
I see, I see.

02:14.730 --> 02:18.610
You seem to be more reliable than I have ever imagined.

02:18.610 --> 02:21.320
No, not really...

02:21.320 --> 02:25.240
I apologize for calling you here so suddenly.

02:25.240 --> 02:30.080
Is there anything I can do as some sort of an apology?

02:30.080 --> 02:31.960
No, it's fine, really.

02:31.960 --> 02:34.380
Just call me if you need anything.

02:34.380 --> 02:36.880
Your own personal basketball court!

02:36.880 --> 02:39.760
A tour of watching live NBA games!

02:39.760 --> 02:43.510
I can even invite the entire Dream Team here!

02:43.510 --> 02:44.220
Huh?!

02:44.220 --> 02:46.680
You're so awesome, Father!

02:46.680 --> 02:49.060
Hasegawa-san, what will you do?

02:50.020 --> 02:55.150
This all sounds quite nice, but I don't really want to go that far...

02:57.190 --> 02:59.860
Um, Fuuga-san.

02:59.860 --> 03:02.280
I have a request.

03:04.360 --> 03:07.450
Make them see that halation!

03:07.450 --> 03:10.870
We'll carry out the oath we made that day.

03:10.870 --> 03:13.960
Spread out, new formation!

03:13.960 --> 03:17.420
We can see the signs as we call out for one another.

03:17.420 --> 03:23.720
Place your hopes in it, shoot, and watch the arch!

03:24.010 --> 03:28.640
I believe in you, do it like you always do.

03:28.640 --> 03:30.310
Leave it to me.

03:30.310 --> 03:36.860
Put your hands on your chest, and calm yourself down.

03:36.860 --> 03:43.150
I remember each and every granted wish,

03:43.150 --> 03:49.030
including that day I cried in secret.

03:49.030 --> 03:52.540
We're not the only ones

03:52.540 --> 03:56.080
seeing these same dreams.

03:56.080 --> 03:59.710
The sparks in those unyielding eyes

03:59.710 --> 04:02.840
that appeared in front of me,

04:02.840 --> 04:04.420
let them fly!

04:04.720 --> 04:07.840
Make them see that halation!

04:07.840 --> 04:11.180
Run into that open space!

04:11.180 --> 04:17.810
This lingering sensation, looking back on those carefree days.

04:17.810 --> 04:24.360
After saying farewell, you smile with everyone else,

04:24.360 --> 04:30.660
aim for the place you dreamed of, shoot, and watch the arch!

04:34.210 --> 04:38.250
Isn't ForM Maho's father's brand?

04:38.250 --> 04:40.300
That kinda pisses me off.

04:40.300 --> 04:43.630
Never mind that, there are special rules for entering.

04:44.010 --> 04:47.350
Teams are limited to elementary girls with 5-player teams.

04:47.350 --> 04:49.140
No substitutions allowed in game.

04:49.140 --> 04:54.140
These rules allow our team and Tomoka's team to enter.

04:55.350 --> 04:57.810
Seems like our chance for revenge is here.

04:59.150 --> 05:00.820
Just you wait, stupid Maho!

05:00.820 --> 05:02.650
We won't lose this time!

05:02.650 --> 05:07.280
But it'll be hard to beat Tomoka-chan's team.

05:07.280 --> 05:10.990
We may have gotten stronger, but they have, too.

05:10.990 --> 05:14.040
We'll still win! We'll definitely win!

05:16.290 --> 05:17.790
I don't mind either way.

05:17.790 --> 05:20.840
Let's start practicing already. We don't have much time.

05:20.840 --> 05:22.840
Y-You don't need to tell us!

05:22.840 --> 05:23.970
We know!

05:27.760 --> 05:29.180
Tsuba! Let's practice here!

05:29.180 --> 05:29.970
Okay!

05:32.010 --> 05:34.020
All right! Gather around, everyone.

05:34.020 --> 05:36.770
I have a special training regimen to prepare you for the tournament.

05:37.140 --> 05:38.770
A special training regimen?

05:54.040 --> 05:56.160
Mini-basketball tournament information

05:56.710 --> 05:59.790
<i>This sounds like a pretty interesting tournament.</i>

06:00.840 --> 06:01.840
Aya!

06:02.300 --> 06:05.300
Aya, we might be able to meet her soon.

06:06.380 --> 06:07.930
The girl you've always looked up to.

06:08.590 --> 06:09.970
Really?

06:12.430 --> 06:14.930
<i>We can finally meet!</i>

06:18.770 --> 06:21.060
Man, I'm exhausted!

06:21.060 --> 06:24.530
This training regimen is really tough!

06:24.530 --> 06:28.400
It's a special training menu
Hasegawa-san made for the tournament.

06:28.400 --> 06:30.990
It's tough, but let's do our best!

06:30.990 --> 06:32.780
Hina-chan, are you okay?

06:32.780 --> 06:33.990
Oh!

06:33.990 --> 06:36.290
If I take a big nap here,

06:36.290 --> 06:38.040
then I'll lose to Kage!

06:38.040 --> 06:41.750
I'm sure the fifth-years are training a lot, too.

06:41.750 --> 06:42.840
Those fools!

06:42.840 --> 06:44.630
I won't lose to them!

06:44.630 --> 06:46.510
Time for 100 sit-ups!

06:46.510 --> 06:47.920
Calm down.

06:47.920 --> 06:49.880
Subaru-san told us.

06:49.880 --> 06:53.300
Just believe in what we've been doing and everything will be fine.

06:53.300 --> 06:54.760
Oh!

06:54.760 --> 06:56.850
If that's what he said,

06:56.850 --> 06:58.640
then I'll believe him!

06:58.640 --> 06:59.850
Me, too.

06:59.850 --> 07:04.360
We got this far because of Hasegawa-san!

07:04.360 --> 07:08.190
We couldn't enter official tournaments,

07:08.190 --> 07:11.610
but now he's prepared such an amazing stage!

07:11.610 --> 07:14.280
We must do our best and win!

07:14.280 --> 07:16.330
Yeah!

07:18.700 --> 07:21.200
I can't go on...

07:23.290 --> 07:24.960
No more! I can't move anymore!

07:29.170 --> 07:30.680
Good work.

07:30.680 --> 07:32.710
We'll end here for today.

07:33.340 --> 07:37.350
We've just been running. Is that the special training regimen?

07:37.350 --> 07:40.230
Can we really beat Saki and the others like this?

07:40.640 --> 07:44.150
I'm sure she made us do this because she's angry.

07:44.150 --> 07:46.360
Masami started practicing her shooting on her own.

07:46.360 --> 07:47.400
Yeah, that's right!

07:47.400 --> 07:48.690
What are you saying?

07:48.690 --> 07:51.150
You two started doing passing exercises!

07:51.150 --> 07:53.410
Mimi and Kagetsu started
practicing all by themselves, too!

07:53.410 --> 07:54.410
What did you say?!

07:54.410 --> 07:55.120
Say that again!

07:55.120 --> 07:56.620
Calm down, everyone!

07:56.620 --> 07:59.120
Relax, relax.

07:59.120 --> 08:01.910
Maybe we should give up on entering the tournament.

08:02.920 --> 08:04.130
Wh-Why?

08:05.000 --> 08:09.130
Only 5-player teams can enter, right?

08:09.130 --> 08:13.250
You girls are all over the place. Can you really call yourselves a team?

08:14.890 --> 08:19.770
If you enter right now, you'll just lose to the sixth-years again.

08:22.060 --> 08:26.810
Can we really beat Saki and the others just by doing these running exercises?

08:27.770 --> 08:30.070
I don't know.

08:30.070 --> 08:34.110
But if you don't do anything, then you'll definitely lose.

08:42.200 --> 08:44.870
We're not a team, huh?

08:44.870 --> 08:46.750
She was so blunt.

08:47.790 --> 08:51.340
I didn't like it, but I couldn't say anything back.

08:51.340 --> 08:55.220
Aoi's comment was correct.

08:55.220 --> 08:57.890
In order to beat Nee-san and her friends,

08:57.890 --> 09:03.600
we need to work on our teamwork as well as our stamina and technique.

09:06.560 --> 09:09.320
We're lacking in lots of areas, in other words.

09:21.290 --> 09:25.460
Elementary schoolers are the best! Oh!

09:55.780 --> 09:57.400
We'll just have to do it, then.

09:58.280 --> 10:00.570
I don't want to lose anymore.

10:00.570 --> 10:03.290
I'll definitely win this time!

10:19.340 --> 10:21.600
6th Years

10:19.340 --> 10:21.600
5th Years

10:36.440 --> 10:38.110
Sorry for making you wait.

10:39.530 --> 10:41.660
Please teach us, Coach!

10:41.660 --> 10:43.330
Please!

10:44.030 --> 10:45.120
You guys...

10:46.200 --> 10:51.250
If we follow what you say, then we can beat the sixth-years, right?

10:51.250 --> 10:56.260
I can't guarantee victory, but I have
strategies in playing them on even footing.

10:56.260 --> 10:59.260
I'll show you the way!

10:59.720 --> 11:01.590
Let's fight together!

11:01.590 --> 11:02.720
Okay!

11:36.670 --> 11:40.510
You all seem to be really into this.

11:40.510 --> 11:42.590
Of course.

11:42.590 --> 11:46.100
I won't deny that there's a difference in skill.

11:47.390 --> 11:48.350
But...

11:49.600 --> 11:50.350
But?

11:51.060 --> 11:53.850
Overcoming that difference is what makes it fun.

11:57.730 --> 12:00.440
Well then, let me challenge you formally.

12:00.440 --> 12:02.950
We won't lose, you know.

12:02.950 --> 12:04.740
We won't lose, either.

12:05.950 --> 12:10.000
I'll show you how a wild boar fights!

12:11.080 --> 12:12.460
Wild boar?

12:15.000 --> 12:18.000
Bust size

12:15.000 --> 12:18.000
None. (Must be a mistake though since

12:15.000 --> 12:18.000
she's pretty upbeat about it.)

12:15.000 --> 12:18.000
Words to Subaru

12:15.000 --> 12:18.000
Burn up! Maho-Maho Beam!

12:15.000 --> 12:18.000
Name

12:15.000 --> 12:18.000
Misawa Maho

12:15.000 --> 12:18.000
Date of birth

12:15.000 --> 12:18.000
Blood type

12:15.000 --> 12:18.000
Class

12:15.000 --> 12:18.000
6th Year, Class C

12:15.000 --> 12:18.000
Height

12:18.800 --> 12:23.680
Let us begin the mini-basketball tournament!

12:27.970 --> 12:32.100
And with that, I'll reveal the bracket! Come on!

12:40.730 --> 12:42.150
Oh!

12:42.150 --> 12:43.740
Yambaru is a bunny!

12:43.740 --> 12:44.860
H-Hey!

12:44.860 --> 12:47.700
Is that what Fuuga-san's into?

12:48.370 --> 12:50.830
Should I look? Should I look away?

12:51.160 --> 12:51.870
Oh!

12:51.870 --> 12:54.080
The bracket looks pretty interesting.

12:54.460 --> 12:59.170
Seems like we'll meet in the semifinals if we win out.

13:03.590 --> 13:06.470
Saki! We only have one thing to say!

13:06.470 --> 13:07.550
That's right!

13:07.550 --> 13:09.100
If we beat you all today,

13:09.100 --> 13:11.680
we'll become the real basketball team!

13:11.680 --> 13:12.980
No problems, right?

13:12.980 --> 13:14.390
Sure.

13:14.390 --> 13:21.650
But if we win, then you'll help us in our training as assistants for a while.

13:25.990 --> 13:27.110
Oh?

13:27.110 --> 13:29.740
You'll order us around like slaves, right?

13:30.120 --> 13:31.290
Oh well.

13:31.290 --> 13:33.750
We just have to win.

13:33.750 --> 13:35.210
Masami's right!

13:35.210 --> 13:37.250
We'll win, anyway!

13:39.210 --> 13:41.710
I'll make you eat those words!

13:41.710 --> 13:44.210
What? You're just stupid, Maho!

13:44.210 --> 13:45.510
Oh right!

13:45.510 --> 13:46.680
I see.

13:46.680 --> 13:50.220
If the sixth-years win, then you'll have a club with 10 people.

13:50.220 --> 13:52.850
That means you can enter official tournaments.

13:53.310 --> 13:55.600
Tomoka and the others thought up of this together.

13:55.600 --> 13:57.730
I don't know what will happen,

13:57.730 --> 14:01.190
but having someone to train with is beneficial to both teams.

14:01.190 --> 14:05.610
But will they actually do that if they lose?

14:07.820 --> 14:10.500
Long time no see, Subaru-kun.

14:11.330 --> 14:13.240
Manaka-senpai!

14:14.290 --> 14:16.790
I've brought the team from Suzuridani.

14:16.790 --> 14:18.330
Let's have fun today!

14:19.460 --> 14:21.040
Is your leg okay?

14:21.040 --> 14:21.960
Yep!

14:21.960 --> 14:23.840
The surgery went super well!

14:23.840 --> 14:26.760
I remember texting Aoi-chan about it...

14:28.880 --> 14:31.680
I wanted to surprise you, so I kept quiet.

14:31.680 --> 14:33.970
Hey now!

14:33.970 --> 14:35.810
But I'm really glad for you.

14:36.140 --> 14:40.310
I'm not at full strength yet, but I'm recovering.

14:42.270 --> 14:45.410
Man, nothing beats playing basketball.

14:45.820 --> 14:48.780
If Suzuridani's entering, are
Miu-chan and the others here, too?

14:48.780 --> 14:52.450
Sorry, they're not in the starting lineup.

14:52.450 --> 14:58.160
I don't want to brag, but our bench is pretty sweet.

15:02.250 --> 15:05.300
She's our renowned rookie.

15:05.300 --> 15:09.880
I'm M-Miyakoouji Aya. Nice to meet you.

15:09.880 --> 15:12.680
Aya was on the gymnastics team,

15:12.680 --> 15:15.510
but you can see how she grew a lot taller.

15:15.510 --> 15:18.680
Then I scouted her for the basketball team!

15:18.680 --> 15:19.980
I-I'm sorry.

15:19.980 --> 15:22.730
I was scouted personally by you, but my basketball is terrible.

15:26.820 --> 15:30.200
U-Um, are you Airi-san?

15:31.110 --> 15:33.120
Y-Yes, I am.

15:33.120 --> 15:34.280
I knew it!

15:34.280 --> 15:38.000
My teammates told me all about you.

15:38.370 --> 15:41.500
There's someone taller than me on Keishin.

15:46.800 --> 15:50.670
I'm sure you were shocked when you suddenly grew so tall.

15:50.670 --> 15:54.760
Feels like the world is running away from you.

15:54.760 --> 15:56.430
You feel scared.

15:56.810 --> 15:57.430
Huh?

15:57.430 --> 15:58.680
Airi!

15:58.680 --> 16:01.690
I-I feel the same way.

16:01.690 --> 16:07.900
I love gymnastics, but I couldn't do it well when I got taller.

16:07.900 --> 16:12.950
I started falling behind, so I wanted to try basketball.

16:12.950 --> 16:18.830
But I'm falling behind in basketball, too. I'm losing my confidence.

16:21.910 --> 16:23.420
We're the same.

16:23.420 --> 16:28.090
When I started playing basketball, I was terrible and always lagging behind.

16:29.670 --> 16:32.220
Even now, I still have a long way to go.

16:32.220 --> 16:34.590
You too, Airi-san?

16:34.590 --> 16:35.510
Yep!

16:35.510 --> 16:40.520
But my height helped me so many times on the court.

16:40.520 --> 16:43.560
I found something only I can do.

16:43.890 --> 16:46.810
That's why I'm sure you'll be fine, Aya-chan.

16:47.730 --> 16:49.520
Airi-san...

16:51.150 --> 16:55.410
I'm really happy to be able to talk to you.

16:55.410 --> 16:57.820
Really, I am.

16:59.120 --> 17:00.620
I'm happy, too.

17:00.620 --> 17:04.580
I want to talk to you more, if we can.

17:10.420 --> 17:11.760
Oh!

17:11.760 --> 17:13.220
Airi's so cool!

17:16.720 --> 17:18.140
Subaru!

17:18.140 --> 17:20.720
Airi said something that cool!

17:21.850 --> 17:25.270
We will now begin the match between Keishin Academy's Sixth Year Team

17:25.270 --> 17:28.440
and Wada Basketball Team.

17:28.440 --> 17:31.730
Please meet at court A.

17:31.730 --> 17:35.320
I'll be waiting for you in the finals, Subaru-kun.

17:35.320 --> 17:38.820
Don't lose before you get to us, got it?

17:38.820 --> 17:40.870
That's my line.

17:41.410 --> 17:43.040
Well then, see you later.

17:44.500 --> 17:46.420
Okay! Let's go, everyone!

17:46.420 --> 17:47.790
Okay!

17:59.430 --> 18:01.100
Oh!

18:26.870 --> 18:30.790
Just be like yourselves and bring out all you've got!

18:30.790 --> 18:32.340
You'll be fine, everyone!

18:32.340 --> 18:33.170
Okay!

18:36.340 --> 18:38.470
Just maintain your rhythm and we can win!

18:38.470 --> 18:39.760
Do your best, everyone!

18:39.760 --> 18:41.390
We'll definitely win!

18:41.390 --> 18:42.680
Yeah!

18:49.730 --> 18:50.230
Tomo!

18:56.530 --> 18:58.530
Mokkan! Saki!

19:03.830 --> 19:04.950
Yes!

19:04.950 --> 19:06.450
So fast!

19:06.450 --> 19:10.330
They're not playing mind games but instead using pure stamina...

19:10.790 --> 19:13.340
They want to beat us using their speed?

19:14.210 --> 19:15.090
Mokkan!

19:15.420 --> 19:16.340
Got it!

19:20.180 --> 19:22.430
Thank you, Maho!

19:25.850 --> 19:27.430
Maintain your cool!

19:27.430 --> 19:30.230
We still have lots of time!

19:30.230 --> 19:30.520
Hina!

19:31.480 --> 19:33.150
Nee-sama! Let's go!

19:33.150 --> 19:35.480
Oh! I won't lose!

19:38.320 --> 19:40.820
Go!

19:49.700 --> 19:53.880
This is a really good game so far. It's basically tied.

19:53.880 --> 19:55.000
Oh?

19:55.000 --> 19:57.250
Huh? The sixth-years are losing?

19:57.250 --> 20:01.510
That's strange. I thought we were up.

20:04.010 --> 20:05.300
We're winning!

20:08.350 --> 20:09.390
Oh!

20:20.490 --> 20:23.990
Are they worried about the score?
They're missing more of their shots.

20:28.870 --> 20:30.250
A wild boar?

20:32.620 --> 20:33.620
Hey, Subaru!

20:34.170 --> 20:36.710
You're focused too much on the details! You're falling behind!

20:36.710 --> 20:39.880
You're at fault here!
You barge forward like a wild boar!

20:44.130 --> 20:48.430
<i>We can do this! They can't match our speed!</i>

20:48.430 --> 20:50.850
<i>I can see them clearly!</i>

20:50.850 --> 20:52.600
<i>I can still run!</i>

20:52.600 --> 20:54.640
<i>Our training is bearing fruit!</i>

20:55.480 --> 20:59.610
<i>We were pushed back last time, but this time we have the lead!</i>

20:59.610 --> 21:02.610
<i>Everything is going according to Aoi's plan!</i>

21:07.740 --> 21:09.080
Good job.

21:09.080 --> 21:11.580
All right! Everyone's moving nicely!

21:11.580 --> 21:13.540
Coach! How were my shots?

21:13.540 --> 21:15.370
My steals were great, right?

21:16.210 --> 21:19.750
You're the best! You did what you practiced!

21:19.750 --> 21:23.380
Can we really beat them like this?

21:23.380 --> 21:24.760
Let's see...

21:24.760 --> 21:27.300
If this keeps up, yeah.

21:27.300 --> 21:31.310
But that won't matter.

21:31.310 --> 21:35.560
We just need to play our own style of basketball, right?

21:36.520 --> 21:41.480
Yes, that's what makes it the most simple and yet the most difficult.

21:41.480 --> 21:45.150
But you girls can do it now!

21:45.150 --> 21:48.490
Believe in yourselves and believe in everyone else!

21:48.490 --> 21:50.370
Okay!

21:50.370 --> 21:53.870
Okay! Time for the second half! We'll definitely win!

21:56.580 --> 21:59.330
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

21:59.330 --> 22:00.880
Rolling! Rolling!

22:00.880 --> 22:03.800
Keep on bouncing!

22:02.090 --> 22:04.800
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

22:04.800 --> 22:07.220
Elementary schoolers are the best!

22:11.680 --> 22:16.690
Our bodies and our hearts are size SS,

22:17.190 --> 22:22.610
but our dreams can be size LL, can't they? Can't they?

22:22.610 --> 22:27.990
Adolescents have lots of troubles,

22:27.990 --> 22:33.580
but we'll overcome them together.

22:33.580 --> 22:39.000
I want to get even better!

22:34.370 --> 22:35.750
Even

22:35.750 --> 22:37.080
better!

22:39.000 --> 22:46.670
I want to see your face when I surprise you!

22:39.960 --> 22:40.630
Ooh!

22:41.290 --> 22:41.750
Wow!

22:46.880 --> 22:49.590
Just keep on spinning!

22:49.590 --> 22:53.510
The Earth is one big basketball!

22:53.510 --> 22:57.180
I'll believe in the future and move forward!

22:56.560 --> 22:58.100
I'll keep going!

22:57.810 --> 23:00.520
Just keep on spinning!

23:00.520 --> 23:04.480
The universe is one big basketball court!

23:04.480 --> 23:07.900
I want you to receive it.

23:07.190 --> 23:08.150
Ready, and!

23:07.900 --> 23:09.740
Pass! Pass! Pass!

23:10.160 --> 23:12.160
Please take it!

23:13.410 --> 23:16.160
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

23:16.160 --> 23:17.700
Rolling! Rolling!

23:17.700 --> 23:20.580
Keep on bouncing!

23:18.830 --> 23:21.580
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

23:21.580 --> 23:24.040
Elementary schoolers are the best!

23:24.040 --> 23:24.880
Yay!

23:26.550 --> 23:29.050
The fifth-year team is getting stronger and stronger!

23:29.050 --> 23:32.430
I must hone my skills as the point guard!

23:32.430 --> 23:36.180
That's right! I'll work on my stamina using this sushi conveyor belt!

23:38.020 --> 23:41.020
Next episode

23:38.020 --> 23:39.730
I"m all dizzy...
